Modifications from upstream
---------------------------
- Client interaction is re-pointed at KewlKlient's net.runelite API shim
  (java/net/runelite/) instead of RuneLite's injected client.
- PathTileOverlay's scene-tile enumeration loop reads the bundled
  CollisionMap instead of client Tile objects.
- Auto-walk support added (upstream is guidance-only).

Tests not ported
----------------
Three upstream test sources are omitted from java-test/shortestpath/:
ShortestPathPluginTest.java, PluginMessageTest.java and
PluginMessageTestPlugin.java. They bootstrap a full RuneLite client
(RuneLite.main / ExternalPluginManager) to exercise the plugin's own
integration points; the kewl shim has no RuneLite application to bootstrap,
so those tests have no meaning here. The remaining 270+ upstream tests run
unchanged, plus a shim smoke test (Lumbridge to Varrock over the bundled
collision map).
